{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand EMS brought you in because you couldn’t get into your wheelchair at home. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I couldn’t move. I was so weak. I’m still tired, but not as bad. I just want to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But we need to make sure it’s safe. You were just discharged a few days ago for a serious infection in your blood—E. coli. Do you remember that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was on IV antibiotics. I didn’t finish the whole course, but I felt okay. Why did I get so weak again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think the infection might not be fully cleared. Your body is already under stress from heart failure, kidney issues, and your chronic conditions. We’re restarting your IV antibiotic, Zosyn, to finish the full 14-day course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So I have to stay again? I don’t want to be here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We want you home too, but only when it’s safe. If we don’t treat this completely, the infection could come back worse. We’re also checking your labs and doing a CT scan to see what’s going on inside."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t want the CT last time. It’s claustrophobic in there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This one doesn’t need contrast, so it’s quicker. It’s important—we need to check your kidneys and liver. You’ve had transaminitis, and we want to make sure there’s no abscess or blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-11-16 00:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… fine. But no contrast. And I’m not staying long."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT is back. You have a 1.2 cm kidney stone in your left kidney. There’s some swelling and inflammation around it, so it might be infected. That could be part of why you’re sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another stone? I’ve had these before. Does it need surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The urology team says it’s not blocking urine flow, so no emergency procedure. But you’ll need to follow up with them after discharge to manage it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. What about my liver? Last time they said it looked bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan shows fatty changes and some signs that could suggest early cirrhosis. We’ll need to follow up with a liver specialist. It’s likely related to your past hepatitis and other factors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. More doctors. What about my kidneys? My creatinine was high last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is 1.1 today—still a bit high but stable. It was likely due to dehydration and the infection. We’re giving fluids, and it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sodium? I remember they said it was low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-11-16 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was 131, which is low. That can happen with poor intake and infection. We’re encouraging you to eat and drink more. It’s already coming up to 134."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-11-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your white blood cell count is up a bit—11.3—so your body is still fighting the infection. But you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-11-17 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? I feel okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-11-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s expected. We’re continuing the IV antibiotics. Also, your liver enzymes are improving—AST and alkaline phosphatase are coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-11-17 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I had terrible diarrhea yesterday—like 10 times. Is that from the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-11-17 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we tested your stool. It’s negative for C. diff, so it’s likely just a side effect of Zosyn. It should settle soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-11-17 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. I can’t keep going like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-11-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The physical therapist saw you today. They think you’d benefit from rehab to build strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-11-17 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No. I don’t want rehab. I want to go home. Can’t I just have someone come to my house?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-11-17 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They suggested home physical therapy as an alternative. We can arrange that if you agree."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-11-17 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s better. I have my electric chair. I just need help getting stronger at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are looking better. Creatinine is 1.1, sodium is 134, and your infection markers are trending down. We’re going to switch you from IV Zosyn to oral Bactrim to finish the antibiotic course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. But you need to follow up with your primary doctor in a week for blood tests—chem 7, CBC, and liver tests—to make sure your kidneys and electrolytes stay stable on Bactrim."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stone? Do I need another scan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT showed a retroperitoneal lymph node that’s slightly enlarged. It’s likely reactive from the infection, but radiology recommends a follow-up CT in six months with contrast to check it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "More scans? I don’t like them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-11-18 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s optional, but recommended. We’ll discuss it with your PCP. For now, focus on finishing antibiotics and following up with urology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your breathing is stable, heart failure is at baseline, and your diarrhea has stopped. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What meds do I need to take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your usual meds—methadone, furosemide, Stribild for HIV, and now Bactrim twice a day for 10 more days. Finish the whole course, even if you feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t get another script for methadone here, will I?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, but your provider Dr. Evans will handle that. Make sure you contact them right after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And home therapy will start soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-11-19 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re setting it up. They’ll call you to schedule visits. It’s important to keep moving and build strength safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-11-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your code status is DNR/DNI. That still stands, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-11-19 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. No resuscitation. I’ve had enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your labs are stable, you’re off IV meds, and you’re back to your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally. What do I need to watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Finish your Bactrim. Call your doctor if you gain more than 2 pounds in a day or 5 in a week—that could mean fluid buildup. Watch for fever, pain, or diarrhea returning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the lymph nodes and liver?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow up with your PCP. They’ll coordinate the liver and lymph node checks. Urology will call you for the stone. And home therapy starts in two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Take care of yourself, and keep in touch with your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-11-20 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-11-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge nurse will go over your meds and instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-11-20 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-11-20 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in before discharge. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-11-20 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it. Follow up, finish antibiotics, watch my weight, and home therapy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-11-20 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set. Take care, and we’ll see you only if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-11-20 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try not to come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-11-20 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2176-11-20 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team is here. They’ll get you home safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2176-11-20 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2176-11-20 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call your doctor in a few days to confirm your follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2176-11-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2176-11-20 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing the right thing by following up. Your health matters."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2176-11-20 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. It’s just hard sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2176-11-20 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Keep reaching out to your team. You’re not alone."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-11-16 00:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-11-20 16:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was readmitted after being brought back by EMS due to inability to transfer to her wheelchair at home, following a recent discharge against medical advice during treatment for E. coli bacteremia. She was restarted on IV Zosyn to complete a 14-day antibiotic course. A CT scan revealed a 1.2 cm left renal stone with perirenal inflammation, but urology recommended outpatient follow-up without immediate intervention. Her acute kidney injury and transaminitis improved during the stay, with labs trending toward baseline. She developed transient antibiotic-associated diarrhea, which resolved spontaneously and tested negative for C. difficile. Physical therapy recommended home services after she declined inpatient rehabilitation. She was discharged on oral Bactrim, with plans for outpatient follow-up for urology, liver evaluation, and lymph node monitoring, along with home physical therapy.",
    "problems": [
      "Sepsis due to Escherichia coli [E. coli]",
      "Acute kidney failure with tubular necrosis",
      "Infection and inflammatory reaction due to indwelling urethral catheter, initial encounter",
      "Acute on chronic diastolic (congestive) heart failure",
      "Alkalosis",
      "Hypo-osmolality and hyponatremia",
      "Severe sepsis without septic shock",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Calculus of kidney",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Morbid (severe) obesity due to excess calories",
      "Asymptomatic human immunodeficiency virus [HIV] infection status",
      "Unspecified viral hepatitis C without hepatic coma",
      "Chronic pain syndrome",
      "Dependence on wheelchair",
      "Thrombocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Diarrhea, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
